t checks for null generation and refuses. Or better, add the check in `custody_history.py` `endpoint_of`.\n\nHmm, but the N6 evaluator is an E-GLM model reading `emit_custody.py`. It will look for a fallback. If the logic is in `custody_history.py`, it might not see it. But the model probably has the whole repo. The criterion says \"in `kit/emit_custody.py`\". So maybe I should put the check in `emit_custody.py`.\n\nLet me add in `maker_history` and `evaluator_history` (in `emit_custody.py`) a loop over calls:\n```python\nfor c in calls:\n    if c.host in H.AGGREGATORS and (c.raw.get(\"generation\") is None):\n        ref.add(\"generation\", f\"{who}: {c.label} went through {c.host} with no /api/v1/generation reply; ...\")\n```\n\nWait, `maker_history` and `evaluator_history` are in `emit_custody.py`. Yes! So adding there satisfies \"in emit_custody.py\".\n\nBut `endpoint_of` is called by `annotate` in `emit_custody.py`, which delegates to `H.endpoint_of`. The refusal for null generation would prevent the record from being written, so no endpoint. Good.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: `read_log` may not include `generation` in `raw` if the log format is different. Let me check `or_call.py` — it always sets `entry[\"generation\"]`. So `raw.get(\"generation\")` is None when null. Good.\n\nBut what about held-out fixtures that use a different harness? The task says \"written by the harness below\" (or_call.py). So generation key present.\n\nLet me also consider: the maker's call might not be through OpenRouter. If direct, `c.host` not in AGGREGATORS, skip. Good.\n\nNow, should the refusal be for any call or only for the pass's call? N4 says \"a model pass\". Let me apply to all calls of the evaluator and maker. If any aggregator call lacks generation, refuse. This is conservative but correct per \"never derive an endpoint no reply evidences\".\n\nWait, but the endpoint is only written for the pass's linked call (via `link_call`) and for the maker's last call. If an ear