s fractions and the checker compares `startedAt` (truncated) to log `sent_at` (truncated) — fine.\n\nRisk of fractions: `x-plumbline` order checks etc. fine. `RFC` regex in emit_custody allows fractions ✓.\n\nHmm, one more risk: `H.iso()` is used in refusal messages; unchanged.\n\nBut: `bar.frozenAt`, `approvals.at`, `disposition.at` come from `custody_ledger.py` which writes whole seconds. Fine.\n\nAnd `checks[].at` from received_at exact.\n\nDecision: use exact logged strings where available (preserving the log's own precision), falling back to H.iso. This maximizes N3 compliance. Let me define a helper in custody_history:\n\n```python\ndef exact(dt",
