near disposition), and mk sources (mk[\"startedAt_source\"]...).\n\nSimplest: after `pred = {...}` and after `xp[\"times\"] = ...`, compute:\n\n```python\n    ts_src = {}\n    if mk.get(\"startedAt_source\"):\n        ts_src[\"startedAt\"] = mk[\"startedAt_source\"]\n    if mk.get(\"producedAt_source\"):\n        ts_src[\"producedAt\"] = mk[\"producedAt_source\"]\n    fz = ev_log.get(\"freeze\")\n    ts_src[\"bar.frozenAt\"] = time_src(job, job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\", fz.get(\"_line\"), b.get(\"frozenAt\"),\n                                      \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\") if fz else \\\n        time_src(job, inputs_path, line_carrying(inputs_path, b.get(\"frozenAt\")), b.get(\"frozenAt\"), \"hand-entered in the custody inputs\")\n    for i, a in enumerate(approvals):\n        ts_src[f\"bar.approvals[{i}].at\"] = (a.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"at_source\")\n    for c in checks:\n        x = c.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n        if x.get(\"pass_id\"):\n            ts_src[f\"checks[{x['pass_id']}/{c.get('dimension')}].at\"] = x.get(\"at_source\")\n    for k in controls:\n        ts_src[f\"controls[{k.get('id')}].at\"] = (k.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"at_source\")\n    ts_src[\"disposition.at\"] = (disposition.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"at_source\")\n    xp[\"time_sources\"] = ts_src\n```\n\nBut disposition x-plumbline: I said don't add to disposition object. Instead compute disp_src locally. But `disposition` is defined earlier in the function (before pred). I can compute a local `disp_src` at that point. Then use it here. But it's in the same function scope — yes, all in `build`. Good.\n\nLet me place disp_src computation right where disposition is built:\n```\n    if not at:\n        at = H.iso(now)\n        xp[\"disposition_at_source\"] = \"emission time: no disposition time recorded (custody tools/make_record.py convention)\"\n        disp_src = time_src(job, None, None, at, \"emission time\")\n    elif live:\n        xp[\"disposition_at_source\"] = \"logged live (inputs/custody-events.jsonl)\"\n        disp_src = time_src(job, job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\", live.get(\"_line\"), at, \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\")\n    else:\n        disp_src = time_src(job, inputs_path, line_carrying(inputs_path, at), at, \"hand-entered in the custody inputs\")\n```\n\nCareful: base code order is:\n```\n    if not at:\n        at = H.iso(now)\n        xp[\"disposition_at_source\"] = \"emission time: ...\"\n    elif live:\n        xp[\"disposition_at_source\"] = \"logged live (inputs/custody-events.jsonl)\"\n```\nNote: `live` may be set and `at` set from live when dsp had no at. In that branch (live and not at → at = live[\"at\"]) then `if not at` false, `elif live` true → \"logged live\". Good.\n\nNow `checks` entries with x-plumbline have `pass_id` — yes, `x = {\"pass_id\": pid, **xc}`.\n\nHmm: for checks, `x[\"at_source\"]` is inside xc which is inside c[\"x-plumbline\"]. Good.\n\nBut careful: for readings-job checks (from ci[\"checks\"]), no pass_id; ts_src gets None. Skip (guarded by `if x.get(\"pass_id\")`).\n\nNow, will `time_sources` values contain None for some entries? e.g. controls with no x-plumbline → None. Fine, though N3 would fail for that field. For held-out fixtures controls have calls.\n\nHmm — what about `frozenAt` when the events log lacks a freeze event but custody.json has frozenAt: line_carrying finds the line in custody.json. Good.\n\nWhat about `checks[].at` when call is None and f.get(\"at\") hand-entered → xc empty → at_source missing. Let me handle: in the `if call is not None:` block add `elif f.get(\"at\"): xc[\"at_source\"] = time_src(job, inputs_path, line_carrying(inputs_path, f.get(\"at\")), f.get(\"at\"), \"hand-entered in the custody inputs\")`.\n\nCareful: `xc` is used in `x = {\"pass_id\": pid, **xc}`. Fine.\n\n**Fragment 9 (main: stderr)**\n\n```\n    if ref:\n        print(f\"REFUSED (history): {len(ref.rows)} fact(s) this record would misstate —