e simplify:\n```python\n    inputs = []\n    for rel in (\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\", \"inputs/custody.json\"):\n        p = job / rel\n        if p.is_file():\n            inputs.append(rel)\n    logs = set()\n    if (ci.get(\"maker\") or {}).get(\"harness_log\"):\n        logs.add(ci[\"maker\"][\"harness_log\"])\n    for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        if e.get(\"harness_log\"):\n            logs.add(e[\"harness_log\"])\n    for e in ci.get(\"external\") or []:\n        if e.get(\"evidence_file\"):\n            logs.add(e[\"evidence_file\"])\n    for src in (xp.get(\"time_sources\") or {}).values():\n        if isinstance(src, dict) and src.get(\"file\"):\n            logs.add(src[\"file\"])\n    for e in pred.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        h = (e.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"harness_log\")\n        if h:\n            logs.add(f\"{ci.get('evidence_dir', 'custody/evidence')}/{h}\" if \"/\" not in str(h) else str(h))\n    for rel in sorted(logs):\n        cand = [job / rel, ev_dir / rel]\n        src = next((c for c in cand if c.is_file()), None)\n        if src is None:\n            missing.append(f\"evidence/{Path(rel).name} <- {job / rel}\")\n        else:\n            entries[f\"evidence/{Path(rel).name}\"] = src.read_bytes()\n            entries[f\"context/{rel}\"] = src.read_bytes()\n    for rel in inputs:\n        add(rel, job / rel)\n```\n\nWait: `add` uses `entries[arc] = ...` and appends missing. For inputs use `add(rel, job/rel)` → arc = \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\". Good, N7 wants exactly that path.\n\nCareful: the existing `ev_names` loop already adds evidence files by name — duplicates OK (dict).\n\nAlso `xp` is defined later in the base file? Let's check base packer order:\n```\n    for n in sorted(ev_names):\n        add(f\"evidence/{n}\", ev_dir / n)\n    ctx = [...]\n    ...\n    xp = pred.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n    ctx += [(xp.get(\"s5_record\") or {}).get(\"name\"), \"packet.json\"]\n    for rel in sorted({c for 