ration is null? Same annotate refusal. Good, and N4 says \"a model pass\" — evaluator. Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check N5: genreply-full — all replies present, endpoints equal reply's provider host. With pin, endpoint = pin host, confirmed by generation provider_name. The check `pin_matches` compares names. Fine.\n\nNow write the diff. I must produce correct hunk headers with counts. This is error-prone; I'll write hunks carefully and count.\n\nLet me build each file's final content for the changed regions and compute diffs manually.\n\n---\n\n### File 1: kit/custody_history.py\n\n**Hunk A** — Call.__init__:\n\nContext (3 lines before, 3 after):\n```\n         c = resp.get(\"created\")\n         self.created = datetime.fromtimestamp(c, timezone.utc) if isinstance(c, (int, float)) else None\n         self.at = self.date or self.created                 # when the answer was given (server clock)\n         self.started = self.created or self.date            # when the generation began\n+        self.sent_at = parse_ts(raw.get(\"sent_at\"))         # the harness's request-send time (host clock)\n+        self.received_at = parse_ts(raw.get(\"received_at\"))  # the harness's reply-receive time (host clock)\n+        self.src_path = None                                # the log this call was read from\n+        self.sent_line = self.recv_line = self.date_line = None\n         self.at_basis = \"response Date header\" if self.date else (\"response created\" if self.created else None)\n \n     @property\n     def label(self) -> str:\n         return f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}\"\n```\n\nWait, in base the line is:\n```\n        self.at_basis = \"response Date header\" if self.date else (\"response created\" if self.created else None)\n```\nYes.\n\nHunk header: `@@ -80,6 +80,10 @@`? Need actual line numbers. I don't know exact line numbers in the file! git apply with plain apply requires correct line numbers... Actually `git apply` uses the hunk header line number