the same arc name (evidence/x.log vs context/x.log differ). Fine.\n\nNow docs update: add a few lines. Keep small.\n\nAlso N3 requires approvals' and disposition's sources: added.\n\nOne more: N3 requires \"checks[].at\" sources — our at_source lives in checks[].x-plumbline.at_source and also in xp.time_sources. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `source()` returns \"file\" via rel_path which resolves; for job / \"inputs\"/... fine.\n\nAnother issue: in build, `inputs_path` may be outside job; rel_path returns absolute. Fine.\n\nNow, the `fz.get(\"_line\")` — fz is `ev_log.get(\"freeze\")`, which is the event dict with \"_line\". Good.\n\nBut careful: `ev_log[\"_file\"]` handling — we now add \"_line\" to events; the `_file` entry stays. In events_log, `out[e[\"event\"]] = {**e, \"_line\": n}` — for \"freeze\" etc. Good.\n\nCareful: `events_log` returns dict with \"_file\" and event keys; `ev_log.get(\"freeze\")` returns dict with \"_line\". OK.\n\nNow the `xa` for approvals: `live.get(\"_line\")`.\n\nLet me now also double check N2: maker-10min, two Maker calls, first sent_at and last received_at 600s apart → producedAt - startedAt = 600. Our code: first = min by sent_at; last = max by received_at. Good.\n\nEdge: `min(calls, key=lambda c: c.sent_at or c.started)` — if sent_at missing for one call and present for another, mixing; acceptable with the refusal above.\n\nNow write the diff. I must be extremely careful with hunk headers and context. I'll use modest hunks with correct counts.\n\nLet me write each hunk and count.\n\n### Hunk A: custody_history.py Call.__init__\n\nBase lines (context):\n```\n         self.at = self.date or self.created                 # when the answer was given (server clock)\n         self.started = self.created or self.date            # when the generation began\n         self.at_basis = \"response Date header\" if self.date else (\"response created\" if self.created else None)\n \n     @property\n     def label(self) -> str:\n         return f\"