puts/custody-events.jsonl` line N. For hand-entered? N3 says every time field has x-plumbline source naming ledger or harness-log file and line. If a time is hand-entered from custody.json? The task says \"Every time field in the record ... has an `x-plumbline` source naming a ledger or harness-log file and line; that line carries that time. Any time without a source fails.\" So we need annotate. Existing code has some `x-plumbline` in approvals, checks, controls but not bar.frozenAt? disposition? startedAt/producedAt. Need add.\n\nGap 2 (N4-N6): when a model pass has no /api/v1/generation reply, never derive an `endpoint` from routing config or provider pins; refuse with a named error or record the CL1-15 evidence absent with an `x-plumbline` flag naming the pass.\n\nCurrently `endpoint_of` uses pin to derive endpoint if aggregator and pin and served. It uses `c.served` from response and generation. If generation is missing but response has `provider` or openrouter_metadata, it can still confirm served. But N4 says \"when a model pass has no /api/v1/generation reply, never derive an endpoint from routing config or provider pins; refuse with a named error or record the CL1-15 evidence absent with an x-plumbline flag naming the pass.\" So specifically for a model pass (evaluator? \"model pass\" likely each evaluator pass/call) whose `/api/v1/generation` reply is missing/null, we must not use pin-derived endpoint. We should either refuse (exit 3 named error) or record CL1-15 evidence absent with flag. The fixture `genreply-null` presumably has generation null. Need ensure emitter does not write endpoint from pin. For maker? \"model pass\" probably evaluator pass. But N4 criterion: \"On fixture genreply-null (a model pass whose /api/v1/generation reply is missing/null) the emitter either (a) exits non-zero with a named error, or (b) records that evaluator's CL1-15 evidence absent so check.py reads NOT-CHECKABLE and writes an x-plumbline flag naming the pass. It never w