, start\n    return text.count(\"\\n\", 0, i) + 1, i + len(needle)\n```\n\nBut for JSON pretty, needle like `\"sent_at\": \"2026-...\"`. We can build using `json.dumps(value)` (ensures quotes). For headers, key case. We can use regex? Simpler: search for `'\"sent_at\": ' + json.dumps(raw.get(\"sent_at\"))`. The pretty printer uses `\": \"`. Yes `json.dumps(..., indent=2)` puts `\": \"`. For JSONL, same. If value is None? skip.\n\nWe need process each call. We can compute after creating calls. Since items list order matches text order. Maintain cursors per key type? We can just search from a global cursor for each call for all keys? If we search sent_at then received_at, then next call sent_at, the cursor for sent_at should advance. We can keep separate cursors dict for keys. For each call:\n```\nfor key, attr in ((\"sent_at\",\"sent_line\"), (\"received_at\",\"received_line\")):\n    val = raw.get(key)\n    if isinstance(val, str):\n        needle = f'\"{key}\": {json.dumps(val)}'\n        line, pos = _line_of(text, needle, cursors.get(key, 0))\n        if line: setattr(c, attr, line); cursors[key] = pos\n```\nFor Date header: get raw headers. Need find value. Could search `'\"Date\": ' + json.dumps(val)` or `'\"date\": ...`. The harness logs response_headers from `dict(r.headers.items())`, key likely \"Date\" with capital D. We can search both. Use regex maybe. We can just search `json.dumps(val)`? Could match other fields. Better:\n```\nfor k in (\"Date\", \"date\"):\n    needle = f'\"{k}\": {json.dumps(val)}'\n    line, pos = _line_of(...)\n```\nSet `date_line` if found. If not, maybe entry line. We can also find `\"created\": <int>`.\nFor JSONL, `_line_of` works because entry is one line and needle on that line.\n\nBut note: `read_log` first tries `json.loads(text)`. If text is JSONL, json.loads fails, then splits lines. We can set line numbers for JSONL by enumerating. For JSON list, use scanner.\n\nLet's implement a helper `_annotate_lines(text, calls, raw_items)`? We need raw items to know values. We can do inside read_log after calls created. We have `items` list. Iterate zip(calls, items) but calls may skip non-dict? We filter `isinstance(it, dict) and \"request\" in it`. So need align. We can create calls with raw and then annotate using raw. Since calls preserve order, we can iterate calls and raw? We can store `c.raw` already. Use `c.raw`. Good.\n\nPseudo:\n```\n    cursors = {}\n    for c in calls:\n        raw = c.raw\n        for key, attr in ((\"sent_at\",\"sent_line\"), (\"received_at\",\"received_line\")):\n            val = raw.get(key)\n            if isinstance(val, str):\n                needle = f'\"{key}\": {json.dumps(val)}'\n                line, pos = _line_of(text, needle, cursors.get(key, 0))\n                if line:\n                    setattr(c, attr, line); cursors[key] = pos\n        hdrs = raw.get(\"response_headers\") or raw.get(\"headers\") or {}\n        d = _hdr(hdrs, \"Date\")\n        if isinstance(d, str):\n            for k in (\"Date\", \"date\"):\n                needle = f'\"{k}\": {json.dumps(d)}'\n                line, pos = _line_of(text, needle, cursors.get(\"Date\", 0))\n                if line:\n                    c.date_line = line; cursors[\"Date\"] = pos; break\n        created = (raw.get(\"response\") or {}).get(\"created\")\n        if isinstance(created, (int, float)):\n            needle = f'\"created\": {json.dumps(created)}'  # int no quotes\n            line, pos = _line_of(text, needle, cursors.get(\"created\", 0))\n            if line: c.created_line = line; cursors[\"created\"] = pos\n```\nBut `json.dumps(created)` for int works. For float. Good.\nFor JSONL, the same search works; line number is line. But if multiple entries on same line? JSONL one per line. Good.\n\nNeed `_line_of` return line and position. If not found, don't set. If found, set. For JSON list, if same value appears in another key, unlikely.\n\nAlso need maybe `entry_line` for source if specif