`_line` won't leak. Good. For freeze, `fz` has `_line`. For dispose, `live` has `_line`.\n\nLet's modify `events_log`:\n```\nout = {\"_file\": None, \"approve\": {}, \"pin\": {}, \"_lines\": {}}\n...\ne[\"_line\"] = n\n...\n```\nBut then `out[\"approve\"][role] = e` includes `_line`. Fine.\n\n#### maker_history\n\nChange:\n```\n    calls = H.read_log(log, ref, \"maker\")\n    if m.get(\"calls\"): calls = [c for c in calls if c.name in m[\"calls\"]]\n    if not calls: return {}\n    for c in calls:\n        if c.sent is None or c.received is None:\n            ref.add(\"time\", f\"maker: {c.label} carries no sent_at/received_at; startedAt and producedAt must be read from the harness log's send and receive times\")\n    calls = [c for c in calls if c.sent and c.received]  # for first/last\n    if not calls: return {}\n    annotate(calls, ...)\n    ...\n    first = min(calls, key=lambda c: c.sent)\n    last = max(calls, key=lambda c: c.received)\n    started, produced = first.sent, last.received\n    ...\n    out = {\"startedAt\": H.iso(started), \"producedAt\": H.iso(produced), \"endpoint\": last.endpoint,\n           \"x\": {**route_x(log, calls),\n                 \"startedAt_basis\": f\"{first.label} sent_at\",\n                 \"producedAt_basis\": f\"{last.label} received_at\",\n                 \"startedAt_source\": src(job, log, first.sent_line),\n                 \"producedAt_source\": src(job, log, last.received_line)}}\n```\nBut `src` defined in emit_custody.py; `maker_history` in same file. Good.\n\nNeed cross_check hand times:\n```\nH.cross_check(ref, \"startedAt\", ci.get(\"startedAt\"), started, f\"harness log {first.label} sent_at\")\n```\nProduced similarly.\n\nEndpoint: `last.endpoint` from annotate. If generation missing, endpoint_of returns None and adds ref. Fine.\n\nAlso `maker[\"x-plumbline\"] = mk[\"x\"]`. `mk[\"x\"]` includes sources. Good.\n\nNeed add top-level `xp[\"startedAt_source\"]` and `xp[\"producedAt_source\"]` in build. After maker c