  if (job / ev_log).is_file():\n        add(ev_log, job / ev_log)\n```\nIf file doesn't exist, don't add missing? N7 would fail if required. But for held-out it exists. For existing job-rejected, if it doesn't exist, adding missing would break. So only add if exists, and if xp events_log exists but file missing, add missing. Let's do:\n```\n    ev_log = (xp.get(\"events_log\") or {}).get(\"name\")\n    if ev_log:\n        add(ev_log, job / ev_log)\n    elif (job / \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\").is_file():\n        add(\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\", job / \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\")\n```\nThis ensures if record has events_log, required. If not, but file exists, include. If not, no. Good.\n\nHarness logs similarly: only if record names. If record lacks x-plumbline harness_log, no requirement. For held-out, record has. Good.\n\n### Packer context: `inputs/custody.json`?\n\nN8 stranger re-derives startedAt/producedAt from harness logs. Endpoints from harness logs and pin in events log. No custody.json needed. Good.\n\n### Docs update\n\nWe'll patch specific lines.\n\n### Potential syntax issues\n\nLet's write the diff carefully. We need ensure hunk line counts. We'll produce a single diff with multiple files.\n\nLet's start constructing patch.\n\n#### File: kit/custody_history.py\n\nChanges:\n1. In `Call.__init__`, add attributes.\n2. Add `_line_of`, `_annotate_lines`.\n3. In `read_log`, set `c.path` and call annotate.\n4. In `endpoint_of`, add missing generation check.\n\nLet's write exact hunks.\n\nBase `Call.__init__` snippet:\n```\n        c = resp.get(\"created\")\n        self.created = datetime.fromtimestamp(c, timezone.utc) if isinstance(c, (int, float)) else None\n        self.at = self.date or self.created                 # when the answer was given (server clock)\n        self.started = self.created or self.date            # when the generation began\n        self.at_basis = \"response Date header\" if self.date else (\"response created\" if self.cre