ne:\n    ...\ndef json_src(job: Path, p: Path, key: str, value) -> dict | None:\n    ...\n```\nNeed `json` imported yes.\n\nIn `events_log`:\nBase:\n```\n        try:\n            e = json.loads(ln)\n        except ValueError:\n            ref.add(\"time\", f\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl line {n} is not JSON\"); continue\n        if e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\":\n```\nAdd `e[\"_line\"] = n` after except:\n```\n        e[\"_line\"] = n\n```\n\nIn build:\nBefore approvals loop, `ev_path = job / ev_log[\"_file\"][\"name\"] if ev_log[\"_file\"] else None`. Add near `ev_log`.\n\nApprovals:\nBase:\n```\n        live = ev_log[\"approve\"].get(a.get(\"role\"))\n        xa[\"time_source\"] = \"hand-entered\"\n        if live:\n            for k in (\"by\", \"at\"):\n...\n            xa[\"time_source\"] = \"logged live (inputs/custody-events.jsonl)\"\n```\nAdd:\n```\n        xa[\"at_source\"] = json_src(job, inputs_path, \"at\", a.get(\"at\"))\n        if live:\n            ...\n            xa[\"at_source\"] = src(job, ev_path, live.get(\"_line\"))\n```\nBut `json_src` uses inputs_path, which may be outside job. It handles relative. Good.\n\nBar freeze:\nBase:\n```\n    fz = ev_log.get(\"freeze\")\n    if fz:\n        if fz.get(\"at\") != b.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n...\n        if bar_digest and fz.get(\"bar_sha256\") ...\n    bar = {\"digest\": bar_digest, ...}\n```\nAdd before `bar =`:\n```\n    fz_source = src(job, ev_path, fz.get(\"_line\")) if fz else json_src(job, inputs_path, \"frozenAt\", b.get(\"frozenAt\"))\n```\nThen after `bar = {...}`:\n```\n    if fz_source:\n        bar[\"x-plumbline\"] = {\"frozenAt_source\": fz_source}\n```\n\nMaker:\nBase:\n```\n    mk = maker_history(...) if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\" else {}\n...\n    if mk:\n        maker[\"x-plumbline\"] = mk[\"x\"]\n```\nAdd:\n```\n    if mk:\n        maker[\"x-plumbline\"] = mk[\"x\"]\n        xp[\"startedAt_source\"] = (mk.get(\"x\") or {}).get(\"startedAt_source\")\n        xp[\"producedAt_source\"] = (mk.get(\"x\") or {}).get(\"producedAt_source\")\n```\n\nChecks:\nBase:\n```\n        if call is not None:\n            H.cross_check(...)\n            at_v, xc = H.iso(call.at), {\"call\": call.label, \"at_basis\": call.at_basis}\n```\nChange to:\n```\n            at_v, xc = H.iso(call.at), {\"call\": call.label, \"at_basis\": call.at_basis,\n                                        \"at_source\": src(job, call.path, call.date_line if call.date else call.created_line)}\n```\n\nControls:\nBase:\n```\n            xk.update({\"call\": call.label, \"at\": H.iso(call.at), \"at_basis\": call.at_basis})\n```\nChange to include `at_source`.\n\nDisposition:\nBase:\n```\n    disposition = {\"state\": state, \"by\": dsp.get(\"by\"), \"at\": ts(at, \"disposition.at\", gaps),\n                   \"acknowledgesUnobserved\": list(dsp.get(\"acknowledgesUnobserved\") or [])}\n```\nAdd source before or after:\n```\n    at_source = src(job, ev_path, live.get(\"_line\")) if live else (json_src(job, inputs_path, \"at\", dsp.get(\"at\")) if dsp.get(\"at\") else None)\n    disposition = {...}\n    if at_source:\n        disposition[\"x-plumbline\"] = {\"at_source\": at_source}\n```\nBut `live` variable defined above. Good.\n\nTop-level times:\nBase:\n```\n    xp[\"times\"] = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if mk.get(\"startedAt\") else \"hand-entered\",\n                   \"producedAt\": \"harness log\" if mk.get(\"producedAt\") else \"hand-entered\"}\n```\nChange to include sources:\n```\n    mkx = mk.get(\"x\") or {}\n    xp[\"times\"] = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if mk.get(\"startedAt\") else \"hand-entered\",\n                   \"producedAt\": \"harness log\" if mk.get(\"producedAt\") else \"hand-entered\",\n                   \"startedAt_source\": mkx.get(\"startedAt_source\"),\n                   \"producedAt_source\": mkx.get(\"producedAt_source\")}\n```\nBut we already set `xp[\"startedAt_source\"]` earlier. Fine.\n\nMaker_history:\nBase:\n```\n    calls = H.read_log(log,