re, prod_where = f\"harness log {first.label} sent_at\", f\"harness log {last.label} received_at\"\n    else:\n        calls = [c for c in calls if c.at]\n        if not calls:\n            return {}\n        first = min(calls, key=lambda c: c.started or c.at)\n        last = max(calls, key=lambda c: c.at)\n        started, produced = first.started, last.at\n        start_basis = f\"{first.label} response \" + (\"created\" if first.created else \"Date header\")\n        prod_basis = f\"{last.label} {last.at_basis}\"\n        start_line = first.created_line or first.date_line\n        prod_line = last.date_line or last.created_line\n        start_where, prod_where = f\"harness log {first.label}\", f\"harness log {last.label}\"\n    annotate(calls, \"maker\", (m.get(\"model\") or {}).get(\"identifier\"), ref, pin)\n    check_pin_order(pin, calls, \"maker\", ref)\n    H.cross_check(ref, \"startedAt\", ci.get(\"startedAt\"), started, start_where)\n    H.cross_check(ref, \"producedAt\", ci.get(\"producedAt\"), produced, prod_where)\n    out = {\"startedAt\": H.iso(started), \"producedAt\": H.iso(produced), \"endpoint\": last.endpoint,\n           \"x\": {**route_x(log, calls), \"startedAt_basis\": start_basis, \"producedAt_basis\": prod_basis,\n                 \"startedAt_source\": src(job, log, start_line),\n                 \"producedAt_source\": src(job, log, prod_line)}}\n```\nNote: In has_send_recv branch, if some calls missing, we filter them out. But if first/last missing, ref already. If all missing, return {} after ref? Actually if all calls missing sent/received, `calls` becomes empty and we return {}. But ref has rows, so main refuses. Good.\n\nBut `check_pin_order` uses `calls` after filtering. If a call with sent missing had earliest start, pin order might not consider it. But ref refuses anyway. Fine.\n\nNeed ensure `annotate` is called on calls with sent/received but maybe no `at` (Date/created). `endpoint_of` doesn't need `at`. `check_pin_order` uses `c.started` which may be None if no Date/created. But harness has. Fine.\n\n#### File: tools/pack_stranger_bundle.py\n\nChanges:\n- Move `xp` definition up.\n- Add events log and harness logs.\n\nBase:\n```\n    pred = record[\"predicate\"]\n    files_dir = ...\n    ev_dir = ...\n    entries = ...\n```\nAdd `xp = pred.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}` after pred.\n\nThen after `ev_names` loop (after violations remedy), add events/harness. But we need `xp` already defined.\n\nCurrent code:\n```\n    for v in pred.get(\"violations\") or []:\n        r = ...\n        if r:\n            ev_names.add(r[\"evidence\"][\"name\"])\n    for n in sorted(ev_names):\n        add(f\"evidence/{n}\", ev_dir / n)\n    ctx = [...]\n    ...\n    xp = pred.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n    ctx += [(xp.get(\"s5_record\") or {}).get(\"name\"), \"packet.json\"]\n```\nWe'll remove `xp = ...` line and add new block before `for n in sorted(ev_names)` or after. Let's insert after `ev_names` built:\n```\n    ev_log = (xp.get(\"events_log\") or {}).get(\"name\")\n    if ev_log:\n        add(ev_log, job / ev_log)\n    elif (job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").is_file():\n        add(\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\", job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\")\n    harness = set()\n    for holder in [pred.get(\"maker\") or {}, *(pred.get(\"evaluators\") or [])]:\n        hx = holder.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n        if hx.get(\"harness_log\"):\n            harness.add(hx[\"harness_log\"])\n    for name in sorted(harness):\n        src = next((b / name for b in (ev_dir, job) if (b / name).is_file()), None)\n        if src:\n            add(f\"evidence/{name}\", src)\n        else:\n            missing.append(f\"evidence/{name} <- harness log {name}\")\n    for n in sorted(ev_names):\n        add(f\"evidence/{n}\", ev_dir / n)\n```\nNeed `missing` defined before. Yes.\n\nBut `add` checks `src.is_file()`. For events log, if `ev_log` is relative path and exists, add. If not, `add` will append missing