no date/created. So line should exist. If line not found due to scanning, maybe source None. We can add fallback to line of entry? We can improve `_line_of` to find. If still None, add gap? N3 says any time without source fails. But we can't invent. We can add `ref.add(\"time\", ...)`? That would refuse. But if log has time but our scanner fails, bad. We'll make scanner robust.\n\nFor controls, similar:\n```\n            xk.update({\"call\": call.label, \"at\": H.iso(call.at), \"at_basis\": call.at_basis, \"at_source\": call_src(call)})\n```\nBut controls x uses `at` field as time, not `at_source`. Add.\n\nFor approvals, we need source. In build approvals loop:\n```\n        live = ev_log[\"approve\"].get(a.get(\"role\"))\n        xa[\"time_source\"] = \"hand-entered\"\n        if live:\n            ...\n            xa[\"time_source\"] = \"logged live (inputs/custody-events.jsonl)\"\n            xa[\"at_source\"] = src(job, job/\"inputs\"/\"custody-events.jsonl\", live.get(\"_line\"))\n        else:\n            # source from custody.json line? Need line of approval at value.\n            xa[\"at_source\"] = json_src(inputs_path, a.get(\"at\"))\n```\nWe need a helper to find line of a value in a JSON file. For custody.json, it's pretty-printed. We can find the exact `\"at\": \"<value>\"` line. But there may be multiple same at. We can search sequentially? For each approval, we can find line of `\"at\": \"value\"`; if multiple same, ambiguous. But N3 just needs line carrying time. Any line with that time works. We can find first occurrence. But if same time appears for multiple fields, still carries time. Good.\nAdd helper:\n```\ndef json_line(p: Path, key: str, value) -> int | None:\n    if not p.is_file() or value in (None, \"\"): return None\n    text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    needle = f'\"{key}\": {json.dumps(value)}'\n    i = text.find(needle)\n    if i < 0:\n        # try without space\n        needle = f'\"{key}\":{json.dumps(value)}'\n        i =