+ 2 blanks + `_annotate_lines` (N lines) + 0 trailing blanks... wait I need blanks between _line_of and _annotate_lines (2 blanks added). And after _annotate_lines, base blanks 121,122 follow → 2 blanks ✓.\n\n_line_of:\n```\ndef _line_of(text: str, needle: str, start: int = 0):\n    i = text.find(needle, start)\n    if i < 0:\n        return None, start\n    return text.count(\"\\n\", 0, i) + 1, i + len(needle)\n```\n5 lines ✓.\n\n_annotate_lines:\n```\ndef _annotate_lines(text: str, calls: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The line each time value sits on, so the record can name it.\"\"\"\n    cur: dict = {}\n    for c in calls:\n        raw = c.raw\n        for key, attr in ((\"sent_at\", \"sent_line\"), (\"received_at\", \"received_line\")):\n            val = raw.get(key)\n            if isinstance(val, str):\n                line, pos = _line_of(text, f'\"{key}\": {json.dumps(val)}', cur.get(key, 0))\n                if line:\n                    setattr(c, attr, line)\n                    cur[key] = pos\n        d = _hdr(raw.get(\"response_headers\") or raw.get(\"headers\") or {}, \"Date\")\n        if isinstance(d, str):\n            line, pos = _line_of(text, f'\"Date\": {json.dumps(d)}', cur.get(\"Date\", 0))\n            if line:\n                c.date_line = line\n                cur[\"Date\"] = pos\n        created = (raw.get(\"response\") or {}).get(\"created\")\n        if isinstance(created, (int, float)) and not isinstance(created, bool):\n            line, pos = _line_of(text, f'\"created\": {json.dumps(created)}', cur.get(\"created\", 0))\n            if line:\n                c.created_line = line\n                cur[\"created\"] = pos\n```\nCount: 1 def, 2 doc, 3 cur, 4 for c, 5 raw, 6 for key, 7 val, 8 if isinstance, 9 line/pos, 10 if line, 11 setattr, 12 cur[key], 13 d = _hdr, 14 if isinstance(d, str), 15 line/pos, 16 if line, 17 c.date_line, 18 cur[\"Date\"], 19 created =, 20 if isinstance(created...), 21 line/pos, 22 if line, 23 c.created_line, 24 cur[\"created\"] = 24 lines.\n\nAdded total: 2 + 5 + 2 + 24 = 33. new = 3 + 33 = 36. Header `@@ -118,3 +118,36 @@`.\n\nCareful with nested quotes: `f'\"Date\": {json.dumps(d)}'` — fine in a diff.\n\nH3: `read_log` — set path + annotate. Base 139-143:\n```\n139    calls = [Call(path.name, i, it) for i, it in enumerate(items) if isinstance(it, dict) and \"request\" in it]\n140    if not calls:\n141        ref.add(\"harness-log\", f\"{who}: {path.name} records no call (no object with a `request`)\")\n142    for c in calls:\n143        if c.at is None:\n```\nHunk:\n```\n@@ -139,5 +139,8 @@\n     calls = [Call(path.name, i, it) for i, it in enumerate(items) if isinstance(it, dict) and \"request\" in it]\n     if not calls:\n         ref.add(\"harness-log\", f\"{who}: {path.name} records no call (no object with a `request`)\")\n+    for c in calls:\n+        c.path = path\n+    _annotate_lines(text, calls)\n     for c in calls:\n         if c.at is None:\n```\nold 5, new 8 ✓.\n\nH4: endpoint_of — the generation-null refusal. Base 219-224:\n```\n219    route = {\"aggregator\": c.host, \"upstream_provider\": c.provider}\n220    if not pin:\n221        ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"{who}: {c.label} went to the aggregator {c.host} and no provider pin was declared for \"\n222                            f\"this seat (custody_ledger.py pin, before its first call); the emitter will not guess \"\n223                            f\"which host answered (custody SPEC 4: a router is not the service that answered)\")\n224        return None, route\n```\nHunk:\n```\n@@ -219,4 +219,8 @@\n     route = {\"aggregator\": c.host, \"upstream_provider\": c.provider}\n+    if getattr(c, \"has_generation_key\", False) and not isinstance(c.generation, dict):\n+        ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"{who}: {c.label} carries no /api/v1/generation reply (null): the emitter will not \"\n+                            f\"derive an endpoint from the provider pin or the routing config\")\n+        return None, route\n     if not pin:\n         ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"{who}: {c.label} went to the aggregator {c.host} and no provider pin was declared for \"\n```\nold = 219,220,221 = 3? Let me count: 219, 220, 221 → I'll use 4 lines: 219,220,221,222. Header `@@ -219,4 +219,8 @@` with context 219,220,221,222 (4 old) and 4 added → new 8 ✓.\n\nWait, does `c.generation` exist for all calls? Yes, added in Call.__init__.\n\nBut careful: `has_generation_key` is True when the log has \"generation\" key; for `generation: null` → refusal. For logs without the key at all, no refusal (fallback to pin logic). Good — matches \"no /api/v1/generation reply\".\n\nHmm, but the bar says \"when a model pass has no /api/v1/generation reply, never derive an endpoint... refuse with a named error\". Fixtures `genreply-null` have `generation: null` presumably. Good.\n\nNow, also N4 requires check.py reads NOT-CHECKABLE for CL1-15 evidence absent — with refusal (exit non-zero) that's satisfied by option (a).\n\nNow, does the refusal break other fixtures? `job-rejected` and `failures/*` fixtures — do their logs include a `generation` key? Unknown! If a fixture log has `\"generation\": null` for a maker call, my change would turn previously-passing expectations into refusals. E.g., `tests/validate_schemas.py` part 3 expects `routing-unpinned` to exit 1 (record written). If its maker log has generation: null... then it'd refuse (exit 3) and the test would fail!\n\nHmm. That's a real risk. The existing fixtures were built before or after? The fixture README mentions `pin-provider-missing` = \"the log names no serving provider (no `provider`, metadata or generation)\" — so its log has no generation key or a generation without provider. And `routing-unpinned` expects exit 1 with the record written; its log must show served-by, so it probably has a generation reply (not null) or response provider.\n\nBut `job-rejected` (the clean fixture) — its maker log: does it have `generation`? If it has `generation: null` but