ket's end-of-job facts and the run-log row. None`\n5: `of that can be read by someone outside Plumbline: it is Plumbline's own shape, checked against a corpus a stranger`\n6: `does not have. custody/v1 (evaluatordriven/custody, SPEC.md section 4) is the public shape for the same facts —`\n7: `who set the bar and when, who approved that exact bar, who made the work, who read it, beside which controls, and`\n8: `what the approver decided. This emitter writes that record from the job's own files, so a stranger with only the`\n9: `public checker (custody checker/check.py) and the files can re-read the job.`\n10: (blank)\n11: `WHAT IT WILL NOT DO.`\n12: `  - It never fabricates. Every digest is computed here from a file that exists; a fact Plumbline has no source`\n13: `    for is left null/absent and NAMED in \\`x-plumbline.gaps\\` with the reason, and the exit code says so.`\n14: `  - It never infers the disposition from the verdict. disposition.state is the packet's \\`disposition_state\\``\n15: `    (written by \\`plumbline_job.py close --disposition\\`). Plumbline's verdict rides only in x-plumbline.verdict.`\n16: `  - It never writes a remedy. A remedy appears (under x-plumbline.remedy) only when the custody inputs name the`\n17: `    evaluator evidence file it came from AND that file contains it verbatim.`\n18: `  - It adds no key outside custody section 4 except under \\`x-\\` (SPEC section 4: producer fields only under x-).`\n19: `  - It never hard-codes the level. levelClaimed, spread, run numbers, evaluators and harness logs all come`\n20: `    from the inputs, so a CL2 record (spread, run >= 2, a different-family evaluator) needs no code change.`\n21: `  - It needs no corpus, no ~/.hermes and no credentials: stdlib only.`\n22: (blank)\n23: `SOURCES, in order of authority:`\n24: `  packet.json                       job_id, terminal_state, outcome, disposition_state     (Plumbline)`\n25: `  iteration-N-eval-record.json      the final iteration's §5 record: verdict, violations,`\n26: `                                    instrument_in_force (rubric/runner digests), pass list  (Plumbline)`\n27: `  passes/<pass_id>.json             each filed pass: status, channel, provider, model,`\n28: `                                    family, scores, void_cause                              (Plumbline)`\n29: `  inputs/<run>.json                 the run file of that iteration, for the evaluator's`\n30: `                                    verbatim quotes only                                    (Plumbline)`\n31: `  inputs/custody.json               the custody facts Plumbline does not otherwise hold:`\n32: `                                    bar file and its freeze time, approvals (each naming`\n33: `                                    the digest it approved), maker model and method file,`\n34: `                                    evaluators and their model blocks, per-pass time/batch/`\n35: `                                    run/evidence file, controls (case files), harness logs`\n36: `                                    (external), retention, levelClaimed. See`\n37: `                                    docs/custody-emission.md for its shape.     (the Orchestrator's ledger)`\n38: (blank)\n39: `    emit_custody.py --job-dir <job> [--inputs inputs/custody.json] [--out FILE | --out-dir DIR] [--print-only]`\n40: (blank)\n41: `Default output: <job>/custody/record.custody.json. --out-dir DIR writes DIR/<job_id>.custody.json.`\n42: `Exit: 0 written with no hard gap · 1 written, but a field the custody schema requires had no source (named in`\n43: `x-plumbline.gaps and printed) · 2 refused (no packet, unreadable inputs, the job is not at a terminal state) ·`\n44: `3 refused because the record would misstate its own history (kit/custody_history.py): a hand-entered time that`\n45: `the harness log contradicts, events out of order or dated after the close/emission, an endpoint that is a router`\n46: `or a guess (an aggregator call needs a provider pin declared before the seat's first call, and every call must`\n47: `be served by that provider alone), an approval by the orchestrating agent or a model, or an emitter tree that is dirty or not the stated`\n48: `revision. A routing request that did not ask OpenRouter for the pin alone with no fallback and ZDR is a hard`\n49: `gap (exit 1), not a refusal: the record is still true, and it shows what was asked. Nothing is written on 2 or 3; an existing record is left as it was.`\n50: `\"\"\"`\n51: `from __future__ import annotations`\n52: `import argparse, json, os, re, subprocess, sys`\n53: `from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone`\n54: `from hashlib import sha256`\n55: `from pathlib import Path`\n56: (blank)\n57: `sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))`\n58: `import custody_history as H                      # noqa: E402`\n59: (blank)\n60: `SPEC_VERSION = \"0.9.6\"`\n61: `STATEMENT = \"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\"`\n62: `PREDICATE_TYPE = \"https://evaluatordriven.com/custody/v1\"`\n63: `TERMINALS = (\"accepted\", \"needs_owner\", \"rejected\")`\n64: `VERDICTS = (\"accept\", \"regenerate\", \"needs_owner\", \"reject\")`\n65: `LOCATORS = (...)`\n66: `DISPOSITIONS = (\"given\", \"not_yet_given\", \"declined\")`\n67: `OUTCOMES = (\"conforms\", \"does_not_conform\", \"unobserved\")`\n68: `HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent`\n69: `RFC = re.compile(...)`\n70: (blank)\n71: (blank)\n72: `class Gaps:`\n73: `    \"\"\"Every fact ...\"\"\"`\n74: `    def __init__(self):`\n75: `        self.rows: list[dict] = []`\n76: (blank)\n77: `    def add(self, field: str, reason: str, hard: bool = True) -> None:`\n78: `        self.rows.append(...)`\n79: (blank)\n80: `    @property`\n81: `    def hard(self) -> list[dict]:`\n82: `        return [r for r in self.rows if r[\"hard\"]]`\n83: (blank)\n84: (blank)\n85: `def file_digest(p: Path) -> str:`\n86: `    return sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()`\n87: (blank)\n88: (blank)\n89: `def rel_file(job: Path, rel: str | None, field: str, gaps: Gaps, hard: bool = True) -> Path | None:`\n90: `    if not rel:`\n91: `        gaps.add(field, \"not named in the custody inputs\", hard); return None`\n92: `    p = (job / rel)`\n93: `    if not p.is_file():`\n94: `        gaps.add(field, f\"named file {rel!r} does not exist in the job\", hard); return None`\n95: `    return p`\n96: (blank)\n97: (blank)\n98: `def digest_of(job: Path, rel: str | None, field: str, gaps: Gaps, hard: bool = True) -> dict | None:`\n99: `    p = rel_file(job, rel, field, gaps, hard)`\n100: `    return {\"sha256\": file_digest(p)} if p else None`\n101: (blank)\n102: (blank)\n103: `def hexdigest(v, field: str, gaps: Gaps) -> dict | None:`\n104: `    \"\"\"A digest someone TYPED (an approval names the digest it approved): copied, never recomputed.\"\"\"`\n105: `    if isinstance(v, dict):`\n106: `        v = v.get(\"sha256\")`\n107: `    if isinstance(v, str) and v.startswith(\"sha256:\"):`\n108: `        v = v[7:]`\n109: `    if isinstance(v, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", v):`\n110: `        return {\"sha256\": v}`\n111: `    gaps.add(field, \"no sha256 recorded for what was approved (a digest is copied from the approval, never \"`\n112: `                    \"computed by the emitter)\")`\n113: `    return None`\n114: (blank)\n115: (blank)\n116: `def ts(v, field: str, gaps: Gaps, hard: bool = True):`\n117: `    if isinstance(v, str) and RFC.match(v):`\n118: `        return v`\n119: `    gaps.add(field, \"no RFC 3339 UTC time recorded\" if v in (None, \"\") else f\"{v!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", hard)`\n120: `    return None`\n121: (blank)\n122: (blank)\n123: `def load(p: Path):`\n124: `    return json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))`\n125: (blank)\n126: (blank)\n127: `def final_record(job: Path) -> tuple[Path | None, dict | None]:`\n128: `    recs = []`\n129: `    for f in job.glob(\"iteration-*-eval-record.json\"):`\n130: `        m = re.match(r\"iteration-(\\d+)-eval-record\\.json$\", f.name)`\n131: `        if m:`\n132: `            recs.append((int(m.group(1)), f))`\n133: `    if not recs:`\n134: `        return None, None`\n135: `    recs.sort()`\n136: `    return recs[-1][1], load(recs[-1][1])`\n137: (blank)\n138: (blank)\n139: `def run_for(job: Path, iteration) -> dict | None:`\n140: `    d = job / \"inputs\"`\n141: `    for f in sorted(d.glob(\"*.json\")) if d.is_dir() else []:`\n142: `        try:`\n143: `            r = load(f)`\n144: `        except Exception:`\n145: `            continue`\n146: `        if isinstance(r, dict) and \"passes\" in r and r.get(\"iteration\") == iteration:`\n147: `            return r`\n148: `    return None`\n149: (blank)\n150: (blank)\n151: `def model_block(m, field: str, gaps: Gaps):`\n152: `    \"\"\"custody \\`model\\`: {family, identifier, endpoint, readOnly} or null (a person / script).\"\"\"`\n153: `    if m is None:`\n154: `        return None`\n155: `    out = {}`\n156: `    for k in (\"family\", \"identifier\", \"endpoint\", \"readOnly\"):`\n157: `        if k in m and m[k] not in (None, \"\"):`\n158: `            out[k] = m[k]`\n159: `        else:`\n160: `            gaps.add(f\"{field}.{k}\", \"not recorded in the custody inputs\")`\n161: `    if isinstance(out.get(\"family\"), str) and not re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z]+(-[a-z]+)*\", out[\"family\"]):`\n162: `        gaps.add(f\"{field}.family\", f\"{out['family']!r} is not a custody family (lowercase, hyphens, no version)\")`\n163: `    return out`\n164: (blank)\n165: (blank)\n166: `def events_log(job: Path, ref: H.Refusals) -> dict:`\n167: `    \"\"\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl, written as things happen by kit/custody_ledger.py. Latest row per key wins.\"\"\"`\n168: `    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"`\n169: `    out = {\"_file\": None, \"approve\": {}, \"pin\": {}}`\n170: `    if not p.is_file():`\n171: `        return out`\n172: `    out[\"_file\"] = {\"name\": \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\", \"sha256\": file_digest(p)}`\n173: `    for n, ln in enumerate(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines(), 1):`\n174: `        if not ln.strip():`\n175: `            continue`\n176: `        try:`\n177: `            e = json.loads(ln)`\n178: `        except ValueError:`\n179: `            ref.add(\"time\", f\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl line {n} is not JSON\"); continue`\n180: `        if e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\":`\n181: `            out[\"approve\"][e.get(\"role\")] = e`\n182: `        elif e.get(\"event\") == \"pin\":`\n183: `            out[\"pin\"][e.get(\"seat\")] = e`\n184: `        elif e.get(\"event\"):`\n185: `            out[e[\"event\"]] = e`\n186: `    return out`\n187: (blank)\n188: (blank)\n189: `def build(job: Path, inputs_path: Path, ref: H.Refusals | None = None, now: datetime | None = None,`\n190: `          expect: str | None = None) -> tuple[dict, Gaps, list[str]]:`\n191: `    gaps, notes = Gaps(), []`\n192: `    ref = ref if ref is not None else H.Refusals()`\n193: `    now = now or datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)`\n194: `    packet = load(job / \"packet.json\")`\n195: `    ci = load(inputs_path) if inputs_path.is_file() else None`\n196: `    if ci is None:`\n197: `        gaps.add(\"inputs/custody.json\", f\"no custody inputs at {inputs_path.relative_to(job) if inputs_path.is_relative_to(job) else inputs_path}: \"`\n198: `                 \"bar, approvals, maker, evaluators, controls and retention have no source\")`\n199: `        ci = {}`\n200: `    job_id = packet.get(\"job_id\") or job.name`\n201: `    xp: dict = {\"job_id\": job_id}`\n202: `    ev_dir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")`\n203: `    ev_log = events_log(job, ref)`\n204: `    if ev_log[\"_file\"]:`\n205: `        xp[\"events_log\"] = ev_log[\"_file\"]`\n206: (blank)\n207: `    # ---- the emitter's own revision (refused when dirty or not the stated revision) ----`\n208: `    rev = H.revision(HERE, job, expect or os.environ.get(\"PLUMBLINE_EXPECT_REVISION\") or ci.get(\"emitter_revision\"), ref)`\n209: (blank)\n210: `    # ---- terminal state, verdict, disposition (three separate facts, three separate sources) ----`\n211: `    xp[\"terminal_state\"] = packet.get(\"terminal_state\")`\n212: `    if packet.get(\"outcome\") is not None:`\n213: `        xp[\"outcome\"] = packet[\"outcome\"]`\n214: `    rec_path, rec = final_record(job)`\n215: `    passes_src: list[dict] = []`\n216: `    run = None`\n217: `    if rec:`\n218: `        xp[\"verdict\"] = rec.get(\"verdict\")`\n219: `        xp[\"iteration\"] = rec.get(\"iteration\")`\n220: `        xp[\"s5_record\"] = {\"name\": rec_path.name, \"sha256\": file_digest(rec_path)}`\n221: `        earlier = sorted(f.name for f in job.glob(\"iteration-*-eval-record.json\") if f != rec_path)`\n222: `        if earlier:`\n223: `            xp[\"earlier_iterations\"] = earlier`\n224: `        if rec.get(\"pass_rule\") is not None:`\n225: `            xp[\"pass_rule\"] = rec[\"pass_rule\"]`\n226: `        for pn in rec.get(\"passes\") or []:`\n227: `            pf = job / str(pn.get(\"artifact\") or f\"passes/{pn.get('pass_id')}.json\")`\n228: `            passes_src.append(load(pf) if pf.is_file() else {**pn, \"_missing\": str(pf.relative_to(job))})`\n229: `        run = run_for(job, rec.get(\"iteration\"))`\n230: `    else:`\n231: `        xp[\"verdict\"] = ci.get(\"verdict\")          # a readings job files no §5 record (kit/plumbline_job.py)`\n232: `        if xp[\"verdict\"] is None:`\n233: `            gaps.add(\"x-plumbline.verdict\", \"no §5 record in the job and no verdict in the custody inputs\", False)`\n234: `    xp[\"disposition_source\"] = \"packet.json disposition_state\"`\n235: `    xp[\"packet\"] = {\"name\": \"packet.json\", \"sha256\": file_digest(job / \"packet.json\")}`\n236: (blank)\n237: `    # ---- subject: the artifact files, by digest ----`\n238: `    files_dir = job / ci.get(\"files_dir\", \"custody/files\")`\n239: `    names = ci.get(\"subject\")`\n240: `    if na