and if the file is not the events log, add it as evidence/<basename>. That covers checks' logs too (evaluator logs). Actually evaluator logs are already in ev_names? No — `external[].evidence` holds them if declared. Not guaranteed.\n\nLet me add both: harness_log from maker/evaluators x-plumbline, plus files named in time_sources (excluding the events log which we add at its own path). Simple loop.\n\nFor a time_sources file like \"custody/evidence/harness-eval-a.log\", the zip arc should be \"evidence/harness-eval-a.log\" (consistent with ev_dir-relative naming). I'll map: if the file is under ev_dir → `evidence/<relative>`; if under job → `context/<relative>`.\n\nLet me write the packer hunk:\n\n```\n     for v in pred.get(\"violations\") or []:\n         r = (v.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}).get(\"remedy\")\n         if r:\n             ev_names.add(r[\"evidence\"][\"name\"])\n+    xp = pred.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n+    ev_log = (xp.get(\"events_log\") or {}).get(\"name\")\n+    if ev_log:\n+        add(ev_log, job / ev_log)\n+    srcs = set()\n+    for holder in [pred.get(\"maker\") or {}, *(pred.get(\"evaluators\") or [])]:\n+        hx = holder.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n+        if hx.get(\"harness_log\"):\n+            srcs.add(hx[\"harness_log\"])\n+    for s in (xp.get(\"time_sources\") or {}).values():\n+        if isinstance(s, dict) and s.get(\"file\") and s.get(\"file\") != ev_log:\n+            srcs.add(s[\"file\"])\n+    for rel in sorted(srcs):\n+        p = job / rel\n+        if p.is_file():\n+            ev_names.add(str(p.relative_to(ev_dir))) if p.is_relative_to(ev_dir) else add(f\"context/{rel}\", p)\n+        else:\n+            missing.append(f\"{rel} <- a source the record's times name\")\n     for n in sorted(ev_names):\n         add(f\"evidence/{n}\", ev_dir / n)\n```\n\nHmm, `ev_names` holds names relative to ev_dir; adding `evidence/<name>` arc. That's what the existing loop does. So adding `str(p.relative_to(ev_dir))` to ev_names works for files under ev_dir.\n\nCareful: `p.is_relative_to(ev_dir)` requires Python 3.9+. The repo requires 3.10+, and base code uses `is_relative_to` in emit_custody.py. ✓\n\nLet me simplify to avoid a one-liner conditional expression:\n\n```\n+    xp = pred.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n+    ev_log = (xp.get(\"events_log\") or {}).get(\"name\")\n+    if ev_log:\n+        add(ev_log, job / ev_log)\n+    rels = set()\n+    for holder in [pred.get(\"maker\") or {}, *(pred.get(\"evaluators\") or [])]:\n+        hx = holder.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n+        if hx.get(\"harness_log\"):\n+            rels.add(hx[\"harness_log\"])\n+    for s in (xp.get(\"time_sources\") or {}).values():\n+        if isinstance(s, dict) and s.get(\"file\") and s[\"file\"] != ev_log:\n+            rels.add(s[\"file\"])\n+    for rel in sorted(rels):\n+        p = job / rel\n+        if not p.is_file():\n+            missing.append(f\"{rel} <- a file the record's times name\")\n+        elif p.is_relative_to(ev_dir):\n+            ev_names.add(str(p.relative_to(ev_dir)))\n+        else:\n+            add(f\"context/{rel}\", p)\n```\n\nHmm but a harness_log basename like \"harness-maker-x.log\" (not a job-relative path) → `job / \"harness-maker-x.log\"` doesn't exist → missing → refuse! Bad. I should resolve basenames against ev_dir too. Let me handle:\n\n```\n+    for rel in sorted(rels):\n+        p = next((b / rel for b in (job, ev_dir) if (b / rel).is_file()), None)\n+        if p is None:\n+            missing.append(f\"{rel} <- a file the record's times name\")\n+        elif p.is_relative_to(ev_dir):\n+            ev_names.add(str(p.relative_to(ev_dir)))\n+        else:\n+            add(f\"context/{rel}\", p)\n```\n\nGood. For \"custody/evidence/harness-maker-x.log\": job/that exists → is under ev_dir → ev_names gets \"harness-maker-x.log\" → arc \"evidence/harness-maker-x.log\". ✓\nFor basename \"harness-maker-x.log\": job/... doesn't exist; ev_dir/... exists → ev_names gets basename. ✓\n\nNow N7 also needs the record, bar, subject files, checks/external evidence — already there.\n\nNow let me also double check the emit_custody hunks' context lines are verbatim from the prompt. I need to be extremely careful, especially with long lines. Let me re-read the base emit_custody.py sections I touch.\n\nFrom prompt (build function):\n\n```\n    job_id = packet.get(\"job_id\") or job.name\n    xp: dict = {\"job_id\": job_id}\n    ev_dir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    ev_log = events_log(job, ref)\n    if ev_log[\"_file\"]:\n        xp[\"events_log\"] = ev_log[\"_file\"]\n```\n✓ matches my hunk 3.\n\n```\n    approvals = []\n    for i, a in enumerate(b.get(\"approvals\") or []):\n        xa = H.check_approval(a, i, ci, packet, ref)\n        live = ev_log[\"approve\"].get(a.get(\"role\"))\n        xa[\"time_source\"] = \"hand-entered\"\n        if live:\n            for k in (\"by\", \"at\"):\n                if live.get(k) != a.get(k):\n                    ref.add(\"time\" if k == \"at\" else \"approval\",\n                            f\"bar.approvals[{i}].{k}: the ledger says {a.get(k)!r} but inputs/custody-events.jsonl \"\n                            f\"logged {live.get(k)!r} when it happened\")\n            xa[\"time_source\"] = \"logged live (inputs/custody-events.jsonl)\"\n        approvals.append({\"role\": a.get(\"role\"), \"by\": a.get(\"by\"),\n```\n✓.\n\nfreeze block:\n```\n    fz = ev_log.get(\"freeze\")\n    if fz:\n        if fz.get(\"at\") != b.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n            ref.add(\"time\", f\"bar.frozenAt: the ledger says {b.get('frozenAt')!r} but inputs/custody-events.jsonl \"\n                            f\"logged the freeze at {fz.get('at')!r}\")\n        if bar_digest and fz.get(\"bar_sha256\") and fz[\"bar_sha256\"] != bar_digest[\"sha256\"]:\n            ref.add(\"order\", f\"bar: frozen as {fz['bar_sha256'][:12]} (inputs/custody-events.jsonl) but the bar file \"\n                             f\"now hashes to {bar_digest['sha256'][:12]}: the bar changed after the freeze\")\n    bar = {\"digest\": bar_digest, \"frozenAt\": ts(b.get(\"frozenAt\"), \"bar.frozenAt\", gaps),\n           \"author\": b.get(\"author\"), \"dimensions\": dims, \"approvals\": approvals,\n           \"publishedAt\": b.get(\"publishedAt\"), \"groundTruth\": ground, \"dissent\": b.get(\"dissent\") or []}\n```\n✓ matches.\n\nmaker block:\n```\n    mk = maker_history(job, ev_dir, ci, m, ref, pin_for(ci, ev_log, \"maker\", ref), gaps) if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\" else {}\n    m_model = dict(m.get(\"model\") or {}, **({\"endpoint\": mk[\"endpoint\"]} if mk.get(\"endpoint\") else {}))\n    maker = {\"name\": m.get(\"name\") or pm.get(\"engine\"), \"kind\": m.get(\"kind\"),\n             \"version\": m.get(\"version\") or pm.get(\"version\"),\n             \"method\": digest_of(job, m.get(\"method_file\"), \"maker.method\", gaps),\n             \"model\": model_block(m_model, \"maker.model\", gaps) if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\" else None}\n    if mk:\n        maker[\"x-plumbline\"] = mk[\"x\"]\n    for k in (\"name\", \"kind\", \"version\"):\n        if not maker[k]:\n            gaps.add(f\"maker.{k}\", \"not recorded\")\n```\n✓.\n\nchecks block:\n```\n        call = link_call(ev_calls, f.get(\"evaluator\"), f.get(\"call\"),\n                         \"eval_artifact\" if n_passes == 1 else None, f\"passes.{pid}\", ref)\n        at_v, ep_v, xc = f.get(\"at\"), f.get(\"endpoint\"), {}\n        if call is not None:\n            H.cross_check(ref, f\"passes.{pid}.at\", f.get(\"at\"), call.at, f\"harness log {call.label}\")\n            at_v, xc = H.iso(call.at), {\"call\": call.label, \"at_basis\": call.at_basis}\n            if f.get(\"endpoint\") and call.endpoint and f[\"endpoint\"] != call.endpoint:\n                ref.add(\"endpoint\", f\"passes.{pid}.endpoint: hand-entered {f['endpoint']!r} but {call.label} was \"\n                                    f\"answered by {call.endpoint}\")\n   