  lines = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    vs = str(value)\n    hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln and (key is None or f'\"{key}\"' in ln)]\n    if not hits:\n        hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln]\n    return hits[0] if hits else None\n```\n\nAnd `rel_inputs = inputs_path.relative_to(job).as_posix()` if under job else str(inputs_path).\n\nNow, for startedAt/producedAt sources:\nIn `maker_history`, add to `out[\"x\"]`:\n```python\nout[\"x\"][\"startedAt_source\"] = first.source_started()\nout[\"x\"][\"producedAt_source\"] = last.source_at()\n```\nAnd in build:\n```python\nif mk.get(\"x\", {}).get(\"startedAt_source\"):\n    xp[\"sources\"][\"startedAt\"] = mk[\"x\"][\"startedAt_source\"]\nif mk.get(\"x\", {}).get(\"producedAt_source\"):\n    xp[\"sources\"][\"producedAt\"] = mk[\"x\"][\"producedAt_source\"]\n```\n\nWait, `maker[\"x-plumbline\"] = mk[\"x\"]` only if `mk`. So `mk[\"x\"]` exists. Good.\n\nFor checks:\n```python\nxc[\"at_source\"] = call.source_at()\n```\nAnd the `x` dict includes it. Also add to `xp[\"sources\"][f\"checks[{pid}/{dim}].at\"] = xc[\"at_source\"]`. But multiple dims per pass share the same source. Fine.\n\nFor controls:\n```python\nxk[\"at_source\"] = call.source_at()\n```\nAnd `xp[\"sources\"][f\"controls[{k.get('id')}].at\"] = xk[\"at_source\"]`.\n\nHmm, but `xp` is defined earlier. The checks loop is after `xp` creation. Good.\n\nLet me also add `at_source` to the check's `x-plumbline` (already via `xc`). And to controls.\n\nNow, N3 says \"an x-plumbline source\". For checks, `checks[].x-plumbline.at_source`. For controls, `controls[].x-plumbline.at_source`. For approvals, `bar.approvals[].x-plumbline.at_source`. For startedAt/producedAt, `maker.x-plumbline.startedAt_source`. For frozenAt and disposition, predicate `x-plumbline.sources`. This covers all.\n\nBut wait, the bar N3 might look for a uniform location. To be safe, also p