n            ref.add(...)\n    bar = {...}\n```\nI'll add source assignment after `bar = {...}`:\n```python\n    if fz:\n        xp[\"sources\"][\"bar.frozenAt\"] = f\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl:{fz['_line']}\"\n    elif b.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n        n = line_in(inputs_path, b.get(\"frozenAt\"), \"frozenAt\")\n        if n:\n            xp[\"sources\"][\"bar.frozenAt\"] = f\"{rel_inputs}:{n}\"\n```\n\nWait, `fz` is defined before `bar`. I can add after `bar`. Good.\n\nNow, let me consider `line_in` when `inputs_path` is `job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\"`. `rel_inputs` = \"inputs/custody.json\". Good.\n\nNow, let me write.\n\nOne more thing: the base `xp` includes `\"events_log\"` when `ev_log[\"_file\"]`. Good.\n\nNow, let me think about `xp[\"sources\"]` for checks when `call` is None (e.g., a model evaluator with no linked call). The base `at_v = f.get(\"at\")` (typed). Source? The typed `passes.<id>.at` is in custody.json. Add:\n```python\n        if call is None and f.get(\"at\"):\n            n = line_in(inputs_path, f.get(\"at\"), \"at\")\n            if n:\n                xp[\"sources\"][f\"checks[{pid}/{dim}].at\"] = f\"{rel_inputs}:{n}\"\n```\nHmm, but the base `xc` is `{}` when call is None. The check's `x-plumbline` won't have at_source. N3 requires a source. If the pass is linked to no call, the base `link_call` adds a refusal? Let me check: `link_call` returns None and adds a refusal if `name not in calls`. Actually:\n```python\ndef link_call(ev_calls, ev_id, named, default, where, ref):\n    if ev_id not in ev_calls: return None\n    calls = ev_calls[ev_id]\n    if not calls: return None\n    name = named or ...\n    if name not in calls:\n        ref.add(\"time\", ...)\n        return None\n    return calls[name]\n```\nSo if the pass names a call that's not in the log, refusal. If `ev_id not in ev_calls` (non-model evaluator), returns None. For a model evaluator with one call and no `call` named, it picks the single call. So `call` is usually not