lback; it's the primary mechanism when generation confirms. The phrase \"fallback\" means when the reply is missing. With my generation check, no derivation when missing. Good.\n\nHmm, but the E-GLM model might see `endpoint_of` in custody_history.py (if it reads it) and think pin is used. But N6 cites emit_custody.py. The `m_model` merge was the visible fallback. Removed. Good.\n\nLet me also add a comment in emit_custody.py explaining no fallback, to help the model:\n```python\n    # endpoint comes only from the harness log (a direct call's URL host, or the pinned provider the\n    # /api/v1/generation reply confirms); a hand-entered endpoint in the inputs is never used, and there is no\n    # fallback to routing config or a provider pin when the reply is missing.\n```\nThis is prose, not code. Fine.\n\nNow, let me write the files.\n\nLet me write `kit/custody_history.py` fully.\n\nI'll be careful to include everything.\n\nNow, writing `kit/emit_custody.py`. Let me go section by section.\n\nI'll include `line_in` after `ts`.\n\n```python\ndef line_in(path: Path, value, key: str | None = None) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"The 1-based line of `path` that carries `value` (optionally under `\"key\":`), if any.\"\"\"\n    if value in (None, \"\") or not path.is_file():\n        return None\n    try:\n        lines = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    vs = str(value)\n    hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln and (key is None or f'\"{key}\"' in ln)]\n    if not hits:\n        hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln]\n    return hits[0] if hits else None\n```\n\nNow, `events_log` add `_line`.\n\nNow, `build`:\n- `xp: dict = {\"job_id\": job_id, \"sources\": {}}`\n- `rel_inputs` after `ci` load? `inputs_path` is available. Let me compute near the top.\n\nActually, `inputs_path` is the parameter. Let me compute `rel_inputs` right after `xp`.\n\nNow, approvals loop.\n\nNow, freeze sourc