l; a reply that is present but names no provider is refused as CL1-15 absent, and the pin is only accepted when the generation reply names it (response provider/openrouter_metadata may only confirm or contradict).\nNOTES: N1/N3: maker_history/evaluator_history migrate a pre-logger harness log once, adding the logger's sent_at/received_at from the call's own response created/Date (whole seconds), so the named line carries the time the emitter already used.\nNOTES: x-plumbline now carries timeSources/time_sources/times (field -> file:line) for every time field, and time_basis keeps the old startedAt/producedAt basis labels."
